//- schema.graphql
type Query {
  group: AdCampaignGroup
}

interface CampaignGroup {
  id: ID!
  name: String
}

type AdCampaignGroup implements CampaignGroup {
  id: ID!
  name: String
}
==================================== OUTPUT ===================================
✖︎ `ClientCampaignGroup` implements the server interface `CampaignGroup` and serves `name` with its own resolver, which only exec time reads: the executor computes it when the query runs. `CampaignQuery` reaches this selection and runs at read time, where an object of `ClientCampaignGroup` would have no `name`. Move this into a fragment and select it there under `@include(if: $__relay_exec_time)`, turn on `enable_exec_time_resolvers_directive` for this project so that normalization computes the resolvers of `CampaignQuery`, or select this inside `... on` the server types.

